WEBVTT

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:22.960
Can you see this, Mom?

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.670
We finally get to sing here.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.920
Sakura, music has the power
to make people happy.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.060
Okay!

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.100
The power to make people happy...

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.900
I wonder what Hayato-kun is doing right now.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>Imitation Girl</b>

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.490
Good morning. Kisaragi Hayato reporting in.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.250
You said you had something to talk about?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.660
Why are you dressed like that?

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.930
You don't understand, Kisaragi Hayato?

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.760
This is my summer house. 
It's for rest and relaxation.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.010
It makes complete sense 
I'd be in a swimsuit.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.380
Is it possible that

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.560
seeing me in my swimsuit is exciting you?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.830
Th-That's not exactly...

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.960
Not used to dealing with women, are we?

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.570
Before we talk, how about I give you 
a good look at me in my bikini

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.970
and make you blush even more?

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.340
P-President!

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.030
Don't, Claire-sama! I untied...

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.260
Huh?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.320
Claire-sama!

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.410
Kisaragi Hayato!

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.540
You saw, didn't you?!

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.090
It was an accident!

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:11.420
I don't want your excuses!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.960
I'm going to knock those memories of 
Claire-sama's boobs out of your head—

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:16.300
Liddy?!

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:22.280
Damn that K-Kisaragi Hayato...

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:23.930
Where did he go?

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.110
What are you doing, Liddy?!

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.180
Kisaragi Hayato is right under—

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.650
Under?

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.110
What's going on here?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.490
A-Anyway, let's get to the matter at hand.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.260
We received a report from HQ yesterday.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.750
It said that during the 
Savage attack last month,

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:58.710
a variable stone was stolen from
 the concert venue amid all that chaos.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.460
A variable stone?

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.000
Kirishima Sakura was planning on 
using it during her performance.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.140
And they only reported it now...

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.580
I keep telling HQ to share all of their intel
with <i>Little Garden,</i> but they never listen.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:20.650
A variable stone is an incredibly rare ore.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.750
There's no guarantee that the thieves
 won't come back looking for more.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:29.410
We don't know who could be hiding where.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:33.600
Kisaragi Hayato, make sure you 
keep your eyes peeled.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.210
We're counting on you to 
guard Kirishima Sakura.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:38.590
I understand.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.920
I will make sure my mission 
this afternoon is a success.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.570
Excellent.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.180
Now, on to private business.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.760
Kisaragi Hayato,

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.940
I want a rematch.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.940
We're having a swimming contest.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:04:59.980
What?

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:01.900
Don't worry.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.740
I've had a swimsuit prepared 
for you, as well.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:12.120
A... speedo...

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.620
This is going to be fun,

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.750
Kisaragi Hayato.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.420
He's no fun, that Kisaragi Hayato.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.570
Hi there, Hayato.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:43.830
Emile...

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.650
Emilia.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:50.500
We don't get to go out very often,
so let me be a normal girl on this date.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:54.270
But what if any of our 
fellow students see you?

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.730
It'll be fine.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:06:00.060
We're pretty far from where 
the <i>Little Garden</i> is harbored.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.970
Anyway, what do you think?

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.990
Do you like it?

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.180
I... uh...

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.930
I-I think it's cute.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.780
Thank you, Hayato.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.930
I'm really happy.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.690
Now, it's time for you to change.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:20.200
Let's go. I've already picked out a store.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.230
H-Hey.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.080
Emil...

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.520
Emilia. Is this fine?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.290
Oh. Yeah, it's great.

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:33.750
It looks really good on you.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.160
You look cool.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.870
I... I see.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.930
What were you looking at?

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.310
I was thinking of getting
an accessory or something.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.750
Plus it'd make for a good 
memento of our date.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.330
I think this'd work best.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.320
But I like this one, too.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.500
How about we get one?

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.120
On me.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.870
What? Really?

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:56.640
Sure.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.070
Yay! Thank you!

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.190
You like it?

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:02.410
Yeah.

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.400
This makes me yours, now.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:06.400
Huh?

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:10.580
When a guy gives a girl a pendant,

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.910
it's a way of saying that
 she is his, right?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.040
N-No, I just...

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.540
I'll treasure this.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:23.500
A-Anyway, how about we get going?

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.960
Th-This is bad.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.160
Hide!

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:35.730
So Fritz, when did you get 
your driver's license?

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.850
When you weren't paying attention, obviously.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.110
Stop treating me like a kid!

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.160
Your head's always at
the most convenient height.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.610
Stop it already!

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.190
That was scary.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.980
Talk about bad luck.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.160
I can't believe we came to the same store.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:53.400
Actually, Fritz was the one who 
told me about this place...

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.470
What?

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.410
I didn't think we'd run into him, though.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.000
Oh, come on!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.470
I didn't know any other stores,

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:06.420
and I wanted to at least go 
on a girl-date with you once.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.620
A-Anyway, we're going to 
find an opening and leave.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.750
It'll be all sorts of trouble if they see us.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:12.940
Really?

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:16.060
I wouldn't mind staying like this 
a little longer, though.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.110
That was a close call.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:23.010
Sure was.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.030
I'll go get us something to drink.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:27.710
You wait here.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.510
N-Nah, that's the guy's job.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.220
It's fine.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.100
An emergency call?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.120
Kisaragi Hayato here.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.680
Did something happen?

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:44.080
<i>We have an emergency.</i>

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.260
Don't tell me, Savage?

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.000
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.560
<i>Kirishima Sakura has disappeared
from her hotel room.</i>

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:56.030
Though it seems that she wasn't kidnapped,
but rather left of her own free will.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:09:00.220
It looks like she turned off
the GPS on her PDA, as well.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.980
But where would she go?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.200
That's what we're trying to find out.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:09.090
Depending on how it goes,
we may have you join the search.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.630
Actually, I'd rather have you 
join in now, but...

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:17.200
<i>President... Is it just me,
or do you sound angry?</i>

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.230
What are you saying, Kisaragi Hayato?

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:28.170
Why would I be angry that you went shopping
with Emile Crossfode while I'm working here?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.760
Uh... I'm sorry...

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.700
You coldly turned down
my challenge this morning, too.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:40.790
Instead of apologizing, make it up to me
by going shopping with <i>me</i> next time.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.770
<i>S-Sure, I don't mind.</i>

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.110
Really?!

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:52.080
A-Anyway, contact me if you learn anything.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.110
Understood?

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.750
I wonder where Sakura went...

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:58.720
Right here.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:09:59.530
Huh?

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:02.910
Sakura?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.220
What are you doing here?

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:07.570
Everyone's looking for you.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.000
I came to see you.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.320
That looks pretty good on you.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.510
Th-Thank you.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.010
Never mind that!

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.090
How did you know where I was?

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.390
You don't know?

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.510
Just in case something happens,

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:27.520
a client can track their 
bodyguard through GPS.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:29.790
Come. We don't have much time.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.970
There's a place I want to go with you.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:33.860
With me?

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:35.510
Where?

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.070
Secret spot.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.060
But I guarantee it's a wonderful place.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.210
Now, let's go.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.450
H-Hold on a second.

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:44.930
What?

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:46.850
You have something to do?

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:48.120
N-No...

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:50.640
<i>If she runs into Emilia,</i>

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.130
<i>things are going to get ugly...</i>

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.500
Fine. I'll go with you.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:59.190
But in exchange, I want you 
to contact Souffle-san.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:00.850
That's my condition.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.510
Sure. Got it.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.820
Now, let's go, Mr. Hero 
of these Zwei Islands.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.930
Could you get us a taxi?

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:11.460
Yeesh.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:15.760
<i>Sorry, Emilia.</i>

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.500
<i>I'll contact you later.</i>

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.450
I'm back, Hayato!

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:21.780
Huh?

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:23.950
Hayato?

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:26.630
A text?

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:28.960
Wait...

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.080
Wh-What should I do?

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.560
Yes. That's right.

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.840
<i>I texted Emilia about what happened,</i>

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.680
<i>but I'm sure she's gonna be mad at me.</i>

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:44.720
Look, I'm sorry I left 
without saying anything.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.220
Yes.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:50.820
I've more or less finished the song
that's going on the album, so don't worry.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>Don't worry?</i>

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.250
Hayato-kun, you explain the rest.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.230
<i>Hello, Sakura? Are you listening?</i>

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.230
What?!

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.830
<i>Sorry, Souffle-san. 
It's Kisaragi Hayato...</i>

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.360
We're the ones who should
 be sorry, Kisaragi-san.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.110
You're having to deal with
Sakura's whims and fancies.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.340
No, it's fine.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.130
Just doing my job.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:09.700
What the heck? You're no fun.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.580
Yes, yes.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.740
I'll contact you about that.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:16.930
Thank you.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:21.790
She wants us back by 
rehearsal, no matter what.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.590
I know that.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.890
Anyway, it's fine. 
Now no one is going to bug us.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.000
So where are we going?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.100
You think you can tell me now?

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.730
I told you it was secret.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.490
Did we find Kirishima Sakura?

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:48.740
Yes.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:53.790
Kisaragi Hayato just informed us
that she's with him currently.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.980
According to her PDA's location info,

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.910
they're heading towards 
the island's Grand Canyon.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.420
Good grief.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.660
What a boob.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.570
Look, Hayato-kun.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.390
Isn't it an amazing view?

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:21.730
Yeah.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.690
That's awesome.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.320
It's the Zwei Grand Canyon.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:30.990
I really wanted to show you this.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:32.160
Why me?

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:37.290
You're the hero who protected this vista...

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:42.110
This precious place my mom showed me.

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.130
Sakura...

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.260
I'm sorry.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.930
When I met you yesterday,

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:56.430
all I could think of was how you protected this place
and preserved my memories with mom...

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:58.580
...and I got kind of excited.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.400
I was acting pretty weird, huh?

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:04.860
Yeah.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:13.690
Hayato-kun, I want to thank you again.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:18.970
Thank you for saving 
something so special to me.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.430
Hey, stop it. I just fought without 
really thinking about anything.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:26.050
I couldn't have won without
the help of the other Slayers.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.350
You're still a hero to me.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:31.300
So let me thank you.

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:33.810
Sure.

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.580
That's a good song.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:56.490
My little sister used to hum that.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:57.770
That couldn't be.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:00.910
My mom created that song for me.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.850
I've rarely ever let anyone hear it.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:08.560
Even now, I only hummed it because
I wanted you to hear it.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:21.730
Hayato-kun, could you
tell me your sister's name?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.860
It's Karen...

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:32.320
Were you in Gudenberg during
 the second Savage attack?

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:32.850
Huh?

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.970
In the shelter downtown?

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.040
Y-Yeah...

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.620
Could you be...

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:47.670
Back then, when I'd lost my mother and was all alone,
this sibling pair told me they liked my singing.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.880
The sister's name was Karen.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.050
I didn't get to hear the brother's name.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:58.700
So it was you, Hayato-kun...

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:07.120
I sang the song my mom composed for me.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:10.710
And in the end, the brother said to me...

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.570
I don't know much about music,

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.470
but your singing makes me feel better.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.520
I can't believe it.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:24.670
I can't believe that boy—

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.360
the one who changed my entire life—

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.030
was you, Hayato-kun.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:31.750
Your life?

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.180
Yes...

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:38.890
When you praised me back then,
I started to like singing.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.490
It filled me with confidence.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:44.100
And that's what made me
want to become a singer.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.510
I never thought we'd meet like this.

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:51.240
I'm so happy I kept singing.

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:57.650
But we only met that one time, right?

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:00.370
You were gone the next day.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:04.370
Yes. My father, who I had never 
met before, came to get me.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:07.330
Shortly after I was taken back to
 my father's homeland,

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:10.500
I became ill with an unknown virus.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:12.630
<i>The same as Karen...</i>

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:19.350
Souffle was a genetic engineer
who was in charge of me at first.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.940
But I didn't get better at all.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:28.170
Instead, I lost my voice,

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.270
and wasn't able to sing anymore.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:36.400
My father, without asking Souffle at all,

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:40.280
sold me off to a Warslarn research facility.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:46.990
There we were injected with a vaccine 
made from Savage fluids,

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:52.190
under orders from the director
 of the lab, Vitaly Tynyanov.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:58.630
Several children died because
 the vaccine was so potent.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:04.160
But I survived and came to
be able to sing once more.

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:08.270
I was saved by Vitaly's vaccine.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:15.440
However, the vaccine continued to be
injected into the children that survived.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.570
What do you mean?

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.530
Vitaly's goal isn't to cure illness.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:25.080
It was to artificially turn 
normal humans into Slayers.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:29.240
Even when we were able to deploy a Hundred,

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:33.190
they continued to inject the vaccine, 
attempting to give us even stronger powers.

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:37.090
No matter what the side effects,
 they kept doing it.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:48.320
Latuni!

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:52.720
Sing, Sakura.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:53.570
Sure.

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:56.330
And I sang.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.920
Because everyone calmed down when I did.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.770
And I sang.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:13.710
So they could feel a little bit more at ease.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:17.510
Over and over again.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:22.350
But not one of them
 made a complete recovery.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.390
Sakura!

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.430
By luck, I survived.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:36.230
My illness was cured, 
and while I can't fight,

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:37.860
I am now a Slayer.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:42.810
I can even sing,

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.950
and be Kirishima Sakura, the diva.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:49.230
But I...

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:52.920
So you're a Variant, too.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:56.130
Hayato-kun, why do you know about Variants?!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:56.790
Oh...

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:59.650
And you said "too." 
What do you mean by that?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:01.840
Uh...

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.850
Well, I'm a Variant, too.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.270
You, too?

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:12.690
Yeah.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:16.070
I only became one by accident, though.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:19.780
Also, I only recently learned about it.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.270
I see...

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:27.130
You're the same as me...

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.700
Wow!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.590
That's great, Hayato-kun!

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:32.210
Sakura?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.990
I mean, isn't it amazing?

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:38.880
You're the person who changed my life,
the hero who preserved my memories here,

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.510
and a Variant who shares the same fate as me!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:46.470
And we just happened to meet again 
and spend time together?

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.350
This has to be a miracle!

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.180
Calm down.

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:53.370
I just thought of a bunch of songs!

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.060
I can't sit here.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:59.830
I'm going to go the concert hall and work
on writing songs between rehearsals!

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:02.120
Hey, Sakura, wait!

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:06.270
Hayato-kun, hurry up!

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.560
Yeah, I'm coming!

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.500
It's good they had a bus.

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:22.880
I didn't think there 
wouldn't be any taxis around.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.560
There weren't many tourists there.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.730
Good.

00:21:26.730 --> 00:21:29.080
It's a special place for my mom and me.

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:31.680
I wouldn't want a lot of people there.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:32.750
I guess.

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:42.400
But I...

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.500
Hayato-kun, do you have a moment?

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:52.150
Are you okay?

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.310
Yeah...

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.040
Wh-What? What happened?

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:57.440
I don't know.

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:02.280
A Savage?!

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:03.920
This is bad!

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:05.970
Everyone get down!

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:14.660
Are you okay?

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:16.170
Yeah...

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:05.740
<b>The Diva's  Love Song</b>
